   "description": "In November 1967, during the same week as her two legendary concerts at Théâtre de l’Olympia, Umm Kulthum granted a rare and intimate televised interview to acclaimed Egyptian broadcaster Salwa Hegazi. Filmed inside hotel where she stayed, the setting offered an exclusive glimpse into Umm Kulthum’s private world during one of the most important international moments of her career.\nIn the interview, Umm Kulthum spoke candidly about her relationship with Paris, explaining that although she had visited the city many times before, this was her first and only time performing there—a dream fulfilled for any artist wishing to appear in the heart of European high culture. She expressed humility and surprise at the extraordinary reception she received at the Olympia and emphasized her constant sense of responsibility and nervousness before facing any audience, no matter how famous she had become.\nShe also revealed that she had received an invitation to perform in London, though the project ultimately did not proceed for unspecified reasons. Additionally, she confirmed upcoming engagements in the Arab world, including an expected tour in Tunisia.\nThe interview covered cultural reflections, French fashion, the simplicity and elegance of French women, and her deep emotional bond with Egypt. She stressed her desire to return home quickly after foreign trips and her pride in Egyptian traditions, insisting that nations should not imitate one another blindly.\nRecorded at the height of her international recognition, this interview remains one of the most valuable audiovisual documents of Umm Kulthum’s personality, offering unique insight into her thoughts, emotions, and artistic identity during her historic Paris tour.",
