   "works": "N/A (final performances: last song sung on November 17, 1972)",
   "locationInfo": "The Maadi Medical Complex of the Armed Forces, also known as the Maadi Military Hospital, is an Egyptian military hospital under the Egyptian Armed Forces Medical Services, located in the Maadi district south of Cairo. Established in 1965 on an area of approximately 83 acres, the hospital was originally conceived in 1961 and transformed into the Maadi Medical Complex in 2003. It is the second-largest medical complex in Egypt after the Kobri El-Qobba Military Medical Complex, with a capacity of 1,400 beds, 217 intensive care units, 37 operating rooms, and handling over 220,000 patients annually with around 7,000 surgeries.",
   "description": "Following severe health complications, including kidney issues and a cerebral hemorrhage, Umm Kulthum was admitted to the Armed Forces Hospital in Maadi on January 30, 1975, after entering a coma. Her health had been declining since 1971, exacerbated by the deaths of President Gamal Abdel Nasser and her personal physician, Dr. El-Zenaty.\nThe Egyptian Radio prematurely announced her death on February 1, causing public shock, but the hospital corrected the statement. She passed away on February 3, 1975, at 4 PM, aged 76, and her funeral was held at Omar Makram Mosque. Her passing marked the end of an era in Arab music, and it deeply affected the nation.Her funeral in 1975 drew a crowd of over 4 million people, the largest human gathering in Egypt's history, even surpassing that of president Gamal Abdel Nasser.",
