   "works": "",
   "locationInfo": "The focal location of the funeral was the Mosque of Gamal Abdel Nasser, situated beside Al-Kubbeh Palace in Cairo. The mosque, a major national landmark, became the epicenter of one of the largest mass gatherings in modern Middle Eastern history. Streets surrounding the palace, Salah Salem Road, Abbassiya, Ramses, and the approaches toward Tahrir Square were transformed into a continuous sea of people.",
   "description": "The procession started at the Mosque of Gamal Abdel Nasser, where the official prayer and initial ceremonial rites took place before the coffin was carried into the streets. The surrounding parts of Cairo were overwhelmed by millions of mourners—one of the largest human gatherings of the 20th century. The density of the crowds was so immense that the planned procession path collapsed, and the masses redirected the route organically as they surged through the city.\nUmm Kulthum, who returned urgently from Moscow (she was supposed to perform there) upon receiving the news, was present at the starting location. The funeral marked a deep national rupture: the end of Nasser’s era and the beginning of the final, more fragile chapter of Umm Kulthum’s life, during which her health notably declined.",
