   "locationInfo": "Tanta Stadium is the club’s most prominent sports landmark, located in the city of Tanta with a capacity of about 20,000 spectators. The club’s physical infrastructure has deep historical roots, beginning in 1928 when the idea of establishing the club emerged inside the “Doctors’ Club,” before a plot of land was allocated to build its dedicated facilities. These facilities grew steadily to include the social building, gardens, tennis courts, and one of Egypt’s earliest swimming pools. The club was officially inaugurated in 1932 under the name “Municipal Club,” later renamed “Fouad I Club,” then “Farouk I Club,” before adopting its current name, Tanta Sporting Club, after the 1952 revolution. The stadium and club buildings have since played a central role in the sporting life of the Gharbia governorate and in developing generations of notable Egyptian footballers.",
