   "locationInfo": "Bosphorus Casino was located at what is now Ramses Square, Cairo, near Bab al-Hadid (the train station area). Entrance fees for evenings were about 5 qirsh. The building no longer exists.",
   "description": "One of Umm Kulthum’s earliest known public solo performances took place here, without a musical ensemble, within Cairo’s vibrant nightlife scene of the 1920s. While the exact date of the performance remains unconfirmed, Umm Kulthum later recalled in an interview from the 1970s that a significant incident occurred at this venue: some intoxicated audience members demanded that she perform provocative songs popular in Cairo’s casinos at the time, rather than her own repertoire. She firmly refused, choosing instead to uphold her artistic principles. This moment became formative in shaping her resolve to protect the value, dignity, and artistic integrity she invested in every word she sang.",
