   "locationInfo": "Suez Canal Zone, Egypt. International maritime passage connecting the Mediterranean Sea and the Red Sea; nationalized in July 1956.",
   "description": "The Suez Canal occupies a central symbolic place in Umm Kulthum’s patriotic repertoire. In 1957, she performed the song “محلاك يا مصري”, composed by Mohamed El-Mougy with lyrics by Salah Jahin, on the occasion of the withdrawal of foreign pilots from the administration of the Suez Canal following its nationalization. The song celebrates Egyptian sovereignty, national dignity, and the role of Egyptian workers and sailors in reclaiming control of the Canal. References to the Canal appear in several of Umm Kulthum’s national songs of the period, where it functions not merely as a geographic site but as a symbol of resistance, independence, and collective pride.",
