   "description": "During Umm Kulthūm’s visit to the Soviet Union, news reached her on the evening of 28 September 1970 of the death of President Gamal Abdel Nasser while she was at the ambassador’s residence. The shock deeply affected her; witnesses described complete silence followed by her collapse in uncontrollable grief. She secluded herself for 48 hours, refusing food or conversation. Out of respect for the late president, Umm Kulthūm cancelled all remaining concerts in the Soviet Union and requested an immediate return to Egypt. A prayer in absentia for Nasser was held at the Moscow Mosque in the presence of embassy staff and members of the community. She returned to Cairo on 2 October 1970.",
