   "locationInfo": "Private residence of the poet Ahmad Ramy, located in Hada’iq Al-Qubba, Cairo, Egypt. The house was historically significant as a cultural hub where Umm Kulthum performed and collaborated with Ahmad Ramy, making it a landmark of Egyptian artistic and musical heritage. Over the decades, the property faced legal disputes, structural neglect, and attempts at demolition by subsequent owners, despite being listed in the official records of the National Coordination Authority for Architectural Heritage under Law 144 of 2006. Partial collapses occurred due to neglect, and the house suffered from fire and structural damage during legal disputes over preservation. Ultimately, the building was demolished, erasing a site that embodied a pivotal era of Egyptian music and literature and the personal and artistic legacy of Ahmad Ramy and Umm Kulthum.",
