   "description": "Umm Kulthum performed twice at the Defense Ministry Club Theatre in Abu Dhabi as part of the fifth anniversary celebrations of Sheikh Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan’s rule, shortly before the formal founding of the United Arab Emirates. The festivities included military parades, poetry, feasting, and special cultural events, with a concert hall built specifically for her appearance.\nHer first concert was held on 28 November 1971, beginning at 10:30 p.m. under the patronage of Sheikh Zayed and taking place on Accession Day. On 30 November 1971, Sheikh Zayed received Umm Kulthum, her entourage, and accompanying artists at his palace in the presence of his adviser Ahmed al-Suwaidi. That evening she performed a second concert, organized as a charity event in support of al-majhood al-ḥarbi (the Arab military effort).\nBoth Abu Dhabi concerts were broadcast on television and are considered historically significant as they coincided with the birth of the United Arab Emirates (the union declared on 2 December 1971). These performances represent her only documented concerts in the Gulf and mark one of the final major international events of her career.",
