   "description": "On 16 March 1967, Umm Kulthum performed at the Port Tawfiq Sports Club in Suez, Egypt, in a grand marquee specially prepared for the occasion. The event marked the celebrations of the second annual Suez National Day, commemorating the 1955 raising of the Egyptian flag over Port Said and the end of British occupation. The concert was attended by senior government officials, including ministers, governors, and the head of the Suez Canal Authority, as well as thousands of citizens of Suez.\nThe performance was broadcast on national and regional radio, with commentary by prominent broadcaster Saleh Mehran. Umm Kulthum sang three extended “waslat” pieces: “Amal Hayati” (lyrics: Ahmad Shafiq Kamel, music: Mohamed Abdel Wahab), “Fat El-Meyaad” (lyrics: Morsi Jamil Aziz, music: Baligh Hamdi), and “Al-Atlal” (lyrics: Ibrahim Naji, music: Riad Al-Sunbati), the final set lasting approximately an hour and fifteen minutes.\nThis concert was part of Umm Kulthum’s ongoing efforts to boost Egyptian morale and national unity during times of regional tension, exemplifying her role in supporting the Arab cause and national identity through music. It remains one of her most documented provincial concerts, illustrating her capacity to unite audiences across generations and social strata through patriotic and cultural expression.",
