   "locationInfo": "Wydad Athletic Club (Wydad Casablanca), founded on 8 May 1937 in Casablanca, was originally established as a multi-sport association during the French Protectorate, created by Mohamed Ben Lahcen Aderdour, Hajj Mohamed Benjelloun Touimi, and other nationalist figures to secure Moroccan access to swimming facilities and later expand into major sports, including football. The club’s name, “Wydad,” was chosen during a founders’ meeting when member Mohamed Mases arrived late, explaining he had been watching Umm Kulthum’s film Wydad; at that moment, neighbors celebrated with ululation, which the founders interpreted as a good omen, prompting unanimous approval of the name. Over time, Wydad became one of Morocco’s most decorated and culturally influential teams, with a massive fan base and major achievements—including domestic league titles, Throne Cups, and continental trophies—cementing its identity as both a sporting and cultural symbol connecting Moroccan and Egyptian cultural heritage through the story of its name..",
